# ---------------------------------------------------------------- private data
# None of this is committed, not even to a private repo. It is the difference
# between a tool anyone could run and a file of someone's personal details.
# (No trailing comments below: git treats the whole line as the pattern.)

# name, phone, email, address, full work history
cv/master.yaml
# the above plus salary bands and a candid list of skill gaps
cv/profile.md
# CV photograph
cv/assets/photo.png
# where you live, what you would commute to, your saved searches
searches.yaml

# Real applications: cover-letter drafts naming real employers, plus the PDFs.
# The _demo and baseline folders are templates and stay tracked.
# _example and baseline hold real cover-letter prose, so they stay out too.
# _demo is a fictional person; _template documents the knobs with no content.
cv/applications/*/
!cv/applications/_demo/
!cv/applications/_template/
*.pdf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ generated
data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
